window.CS_CAMPAIGN_ODV_MATRICES = {"krynn__v3___the_five_book_odyssey__346_352_ac_":{"label":"Krynn (V3): The Five-Book Odyssey (346–352 AC)","match":"krynn__v3___the_five_book_odyssey__346_352_ac_|Krynn_V3_Five_Book_Odyssey","matrix":{"[1, 1, 1]":{"s":1,"e":1,"c":1,"tag":"[1, 1, 1]","archetypeName":"The Sealed Chronicle","coreBoon":"**The Unaltered Record:** Every birth, war and treaty on Krynn is shelved without gloss; no fire, flood or forged ledger corrupts what the Library holds.","coreBurden":"**Witness Without Hands:** Sworn never to warn, intervene or take sides; will watch a city burn and note the hour.","microPassive":"**Cloister Silence:** Inside the walls voices drop, steel stays sheathed and tempers cool; raised voices, open flame and spilled ink carry grave social and mystical penalties.","macroPassive":"**Stillwater Neutrality:** Approaches to the Library stay untouched by raiders and tax-farmers; scholars pass freely, but anyone who petitions the Chronicle to alter an entry is turned from the gate.","exemplarNpc":"**Astinus of Palanthas, Master of the Chronicle**<br>*\"I record what is, not what is asked.\"* Keeps his pen moving while the party pleads, and answers any request for aid with a question about the date. Trades a copied page for an eyewitness account he has not yet written down.","genericName":"The Sealed Monolith","occupant":"Aesthetic Order of Gilean / Great Library of Palanthas","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.2; AC-03 §1.3","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 1, 2]":{"s":1,"e":1,"c":2,"tag":"[1, 1, 2]","archetypeName":"The Blood-Oath Tribes","coreBoon":"**Ancestral Endurance:** Survival trials and inherited oath-law let each band outlast winter, drought and goblin raids with no central granary or court.","coreBurden":"**Orthodox Stoning:** Divine proof that contradicts tribal doctrine is judged witchcraft first; the bearer is punished before the claim is weighed.","microPassive":"**Law of the Circle:** Within the sacred circle, tribal custom binds every member; sworn warriors ignore fear and pain while acting on precedent, and freeze when no precedent exists.","macroPassive":"**Grass-Sea Interdict:** Outsiders crossing the plains are shadowed by scouts; unmarked armed strangers are driven off, while those who speak the hospitality-oath are fed and watched.","exemplarNpc":"**Chieftain Arrowhead, Keeper of the Blood-Oath**<br>*\"Bring me proof the old gods live, or do not ask for my daughter.\"* Sets an impossible quest to be rid of an unwelcome suitor, then answers the miracle that fulfils it with a stone-throwing mob.","genericName":"The Autonomous Cloister","occupant":"Que-Shu plainsmen (tribal law, chieftain's line, spirit shamanate)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.2; AC-04","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 1, 3]":{"s":1,"e":1,"c":3,"tag":"[1, 1, 3]","archetypeName":"The Mountain Sealed","coreBoon":"**Impregnable Depths:** Gates, aqueducts, mushroom terraces and the great lift keep a whole nation fed and warded for generations without surface contact.","coreBurden":"**The Deadlock of Gates:** Five-clan majorities and a throne that needs a lost hammer let any urgent outside matter rot in committee while the surface burns.","microPassive":"**Stone Order:** Clan quarters, rank and ritual are fixed in granite; within the Life-Tree, defense and craft output double, but no innovation passes a clan thane's veto.","macroPassive":"**The Closed Mountain:** The Kharolis foothills fall under a sealed-gate doctrine; refugees, envoys and relics are held at the threshold until a vote that may never come.","exemplarNpc":"**Thane Hornfel Kytur, Hylar Lord of the Life-Tree**<br>*\"Shelter for ninety days, then the South Gate. Not one day more.\"* Offers conditional refuge on written oath and will not allow a single hearth to be lit permanently within the mountain.","genericName":"The Sanctum Bastion","occupant":"Thorbardin and the Council of the Thanes (Hylar-led Life-Tree)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §2; AC-04 §4.2","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 1, 4]":{"s":1,"e":1,"c":4,"tag":"[1, 1, 4]","archetypeName":"The Dreaming Court","coreBoon":"**Total Elven Unison:** Houses Royal, Protector, Mystic, Gardener and Mason move as one will; no dissent, crime or discord survives inside the marble.","coreBurden":"**One Mind, One Wound:** The realm is bound to its king's mind; a single corrupting influence in the seat of power poisons every grove, tower and sleeper at once.","microPassive":"**Shared Dream:** Court, caste and kin feel what the crown feels; morale and pain are distributed across the whole population, for ill as well as good.","macroPassive":"**Marble Quarantine:** Foreign aid, trade and counsel are refused at the border; strangers within the realm are gently disoriented as the court's single voice drowns their own thoughts.","exemplarNpc":"**Lorac Caladon, Speaker of the Stars**<br>*\"Our silence is not weakness. It is the only wall that holds.\"* Receives rescuers as intruders; if pressed he reaches for the artifact that will let him seal the forest forever.","genericName":"The Monastic Hive","occupant":"Silvanesti kingdom under Lorac Caladon (House Royal through House Mason)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §4; AC-04 §4.3","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 2, 1]":{"s":1,"e":2,"c":1,"tag":"[1, 2, 1]","archetypeName":"The Cursed Warden","coreBoon":"**Unsleeping Vigil:** Nothing living can bribe, tire or charm the keep's undead garrison; no ambush survives its line of sight.","coreBurden":"**Oath Without Mercy:** Cannot form alliances, forgive or be forgiven; every envoy is treated with the same lethal suspicion as a raider.","microPassive":"**Deathless Duty:** Skeletal sentinels and banshees ignore morale, fatigue and mental influence; each acts only on its last sworn command.","macroPassive":"**Zone of Cold Interdiction:** The approaches to the keep carry a creeping dread; unannounced crossings of its border are met by wailing escorts and lethal pursuit.","exemplarNpc":"**Lord Soth, Death Knight of Dargaard**<br>*\"My oath was broken. Yours will not be.\"* Receives a courier in silence, accepts no gift, and sets a single impossible condition for passage that only his old vow could satisfy.","genericName":"The Hermit Sentinel","occupant":"Dargaard Keep: Lord Soth and his banshee escort","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.5; AC-03 §3.5","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 2, 2]":{"s":1,"e":2,"c":2,"tag":"[1, 2, 2]","archetypeName":"The Drowned Sanctuary","coreBoon":"**Mercy Behind the Veil:** Rescues drowning sailors and shelters them, guaranteeing survival for the lost while the sanctuary itself stays hidden.","coreBurden":"**The Draught of Forgetting:** Cannot admit a surface visitor without stripping their memory; any exchange of real knowledge is traded away at the shore.","microPassive":"**Tidal Custom:** Coral Guard and war-shark riders hold the sunken palaces under unchanging reef law; members' defenses halve incoming harm within their reef-walls.","macroPassive":"**Pelagic Exclusion:** The nearby sea is cleared of foreign wrecks and salvage divers; approaching ships find kind currents or drowning ones, depending on their reputation with the court.","exemplarNpc":"**Apoletta, Speaker of the Dimernesti**<br>*\"You may live. You will not remember.\"* Welcomes a half-drowned stranger with kindness and a cup of herbal draught, and will accept payment only in terrestrial pipeleaf or a forgotten oath.","genericName":"The Fortified Enclave","occupant":"Dimernesti (sea elves) beneath the Blood Sea Maelstrom","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.3 (source scored [1,2,2])","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 2, 3]":{"s":1,"e":2,"c":3,"tag":"[1, 2, 3]","archetypeName":"The Measure-Bound Knights","coreBoon":"**Unbroken Front:** Interlocking Orders and the 37 volumes of the Measure give every knight a place in the line and a precedent for every decision.","coreBurden":"**The Letter Over the Spirit:** Cannot adapt a maneuver or recognize a worthy man who lacks a pedigree; doctrine outranks the field.","microPassive":"**Interlocking Ranks:** Adjacent knights grant compounding armor and morale bonuses; movement is capped to the slowest rank and retreat requires a precedent.","macroPassive":"**The Cordon of Honor:** Passes and high roads are held by knightly checkpoints that turn back irregular wanderers and demand heraldic proof from every passer-by.","exemplarNpc":"**Derek Crownguard, Knight of the Rose**<br>*\"If it is not in the Measure, it is not honor.\"* Dismisses a field report of a flanking force because the foe must meet the center spear; will not recognize a squire without ancestral armor.","genericName":"The Phalanx League","occupant":"Knights of Solamnia, Crownguard literalists (Order of the Rose)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §8 (Measure vs Code)","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 2, 4]":{"s":1,"e":2,"c":4,"tag":"[1, 2, 4]","archetypeName":"The Exodus Column","coreBoon":"**Total Mobilization:** Every elf, noble and craftsman marches as one column; no stragglers, no desertions, no private grief delays the retreat.","coreBurden":"**Purity Purge:** Half-elves, humans and doubters are expelled or sacrificed; original thinkers are silenced to preserve the column's single will.","microPassive":"**Iron Silence:** Marchers are immune to panic and propaganda; a whispered doubt is treated as treason and answered with immediate exile.","macroPassive":"**Scorched Withdrawal:** The land left behind is stripped of grain, bridges and shelter so pursuers starve; neighboring human villages are warned off, or ignored.","exemplarNpc":"**Crown Prince Porthios, Marshal of the Qualinesti Withdrawal**<br>*\"Burn what we cannot carry. Leave nothing for the dragon.\"* Weighs every human refugee as a ration to be saved or spent, and will not allow a half-elf near the royal banners.","genericName":"The Totalitarian Commune","occupant":"Qualinesti under Porthios's martial hawks (crisis-mode of the Court of the Sun)","sourceStatus":"crisis-state","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.3; WN-01 §6","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 3, 1]":{"s":1,"e":3,"c":1,"tag":"[1, 3, 1]","archetypeName":"The Tithe-Vault of Belzor","coreBoon":"**Sealed Ledgers:** Every tithe, indulgence and confiscated estate is recorded in iron-bound books; a debt written here cannot be argued away.","coreBurden":"**Fear of the Stage Machinery:** The whole edifice rests on hidden steam, mirrors and mechanisms; exposure of one trick would collapse the faith and its income.","microPassive":"**Ironclad Orthodoxy:** Internal rites, accounts and sermons cannot be amended; priests are protected from prosecution by the temple's own tribunal.","macroPassive":"**Liens of the Faithful:** Debts and confessions radiate outward; defaulters in nearby villages find property seized, names read from the pulpit and witch-hunters at their doors.","exemplarNpc":"**Judith, Zealot of the Belzor Priesthood**<br>*\"The faithful pay. The faithless are found.\"* Accepts donations in steel and offers a sworn confession in exchange for a rival mage's name; reacts with blind fury to any hint of the mechanism beneath the altar.","genericName":"The Vault of Records","occupant":"Temple of Belzor, Haven (priesthood, tithes, estate-confiscation rolls)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.2, §3.2","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 3, 2]":{"s":1,"e":3,"c":2,"tag":"[1, 3, 2]","archetypeName":"The Guild-City Cartel","coreBoon":"**The Hope's End Mark:** Standardized quality, apprentice charters and fixed wages make any article stamped here worth a premium in every market.","coreBurden":"**Monopoly Under Siege:** Cannot adapt trade rules or tolerate rival makers; when gate taxes break the system the guild would sooner revolt than reform.","microPassive":"**Masterpiece Standard:** Goods and arms made under the guild stamp are exceptionally reliable; unlicensed tools are forbidden inside the walls.","macroPassive":"**Charter Embargo:** The surrounding region's craftsmen must pay for the stamp or lose access to the city's markets, bridges and warehouse space.","exemplarNpc":"**The Lord Mayor of Hope's End, Chair of the Revolutionary Council**<br>*\"If it bears our mark, it is worth the price. If not, it is not worth the road.\"* Receives the party at midnight in a bedchamber, demanding proof of a sworn oath before he will admit a single armed stranger.","genericName":"The Guild Cartel","occupant":"Hope's End Merchants Guild and Revolutionary Council","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"BA-01 §2 Faction 2","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 3, 3]":{"s":1,"e":3,"c":3,"tag":"[1, 3, 3]","archetypeName":"The Gate-Tax Combine","coreBoon":"**Toll-Road Order:** A single decree funds a chain of gate-houses, collectors and guards; road traffic is predictable and revenue never fails.","coreBurden":"**Overhead of Fear:** The system cannot reduce its take in lean years; a 25 percent tax on raw goods and finished wares strangles the very industries it feeds.","microPassive":"**Synchronized Throughput:** Gate-keepers, tally clerks and tax-sergeants work to a single timetable; evasion is detected quickly and punished identically.","macroPassive":"**Corridor Squeeze:** The tax radiates into every market on the road, ruining small trade, hollowing guild cities and funneling steel to a hidden master.","exemplarNpc":"**King Wilhelm of Blödehelm (the impostor), Crown of the Gate-Tax**<br>*\"The tax is the king's will. The king is well.\"* Signs decrees from a locked room; the royal seal is genuine, the king is not.","genericName":"The Commercial Combine","occupant":"Impostor court of 'Good King' Wilhelm of Blödehelm (toll gates, tax collectors, guard network)","sourceStatus":"derived","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"BA-01 §2 Faction 2–3","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 3, 4]":{"s":1,"e":3,"c":4,"tag":"[1, 3, 4]","archetypeName":"The Steel Treasury of Sanction","coreBoon":"**Punctual Pay:** Troops, smiths and suppliers are paid in steel on time, buying obedience that conquest alone cannot.","coreBurden":"**Cascade Fragility:** Foundries, slave markets and temple tithes feed each other; a single burned forge or lost shipment starves the whole machine.","microPassive":"**Chartered Immunity:** Officers, paymasters and clerics are shielded from prosecution by layered temple and army tribunals.","macroPassive":"**Economic Asphyxiation:** Steel and slaves flow to allies and are denied to rivals; border cities that refuse the Queen's coin find their grain, iron and timber embargoed.","exemplarNpc":"**High Cleric Wyrllish, Keeper of the Temple Coffers**<br>*\"The Queen pays what she owes. The Queen collects what she is owed.\"* Pays a mercenary promptly and then notes the debt the mercenary now owes the Queen.","genericName":"The Corporate Directorate","occupant":"Temple of Luerkhisis treasury and Sanction foundries underwriting the Dragonarmies","sourceStatus":"derived","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"BA-01 §2 Faction 3; AC-03","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 4, 1]":{"s":1,"e":4,"c":1,"tag":"[1, 4, 1]","archetypeName":"The Pax Tharkas Mines","coreBoon":"**Maximized Extraction:** Hundreds of slaves, whip-sergeants and ore carts turn a mountain into iron for the central armies with almost no investment.","coreBurden":"**Simmering Revolt:** Slaves foul tools, steal keys and plan the overseer's death; one spark from outside can turn the mine into a riot.","microPassive":"**Coerced Quota:** Output is high and morale low; every worker knows the price of failure, and every overseer knows the price of mercy.","macroPassive":"**Strip-Mined Frontier:** Surrounding slopes are felled for props and fuel; refugees stream out in every direction while villages are raided for fresh labor.","exemplarNpc":"**Fewmaster Toede, Overseer of the Pax Tharkas Works**<br>*\"Quota, or the whip. The Highlord is watching.\"* Accepts a bribe of Solace beer or forged transit papers; screams for his guards if anyone threatens him in private.","genericName":"The Penal Workhouse","occupant":"Red Wing slave-mines and hobgoblin taskmasters at Pax Tharkas","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.5","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 4, 2]":{"s":1,"e":4,"c":2,"tag":"[1, 4, 2]","archetypeName":"The Daergar Quarry-State","coreBoon":"**Bottomless Stone:** Slave gangs cut and haul stone, ore and fuel for the mountain at a cost counted only in lives.","coreBurden":"**Spite as Policy:** Contempt for allies and subjects makes them poor negotiators and quick to betray any bargain that offers no cruelty.","microPassive":"**Overseer's Law:** Unlicensed rest, speech or smuggling in the pits are punished at once; slaves and slavers alike know the next blow's location.","macroPassive":"**Shaft-Line Pressure:** Lower tunnels are claimed and held with chain gangs and cult-shrines, pushing rival clans out of the deep roads.","exemplarNpc":"**A Daergar Quarry-Master, Taskmaster of the Deep Roads**<br>*\"The stone does not complain. Neither will you.\"* Offers cheap ore on the condition that the party recover three escaped slaves from the lower galleries.","genericName":"The Armament Mill","occupant":"Daergar dark dwarves (slave-quarries, blood-cults) in Thorbardin","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §2 (Daergar)","exemplarInvented":true},"[1, 4, 3]":{"s":1,"e":4,"c":3,"tag":"[1, 4, 3]","archetypeName":"The Red Wing Legion","coreBoon":"**Disciplined Terror:** Synchronized thrusts, dragonfear and draconian shock troops break fortified positions in days instead of seasons.","coreBurden":"**Fragile Supply Spine:** Cohorts cannot forage or improvise; cut the convoy road, kill the cleric or drop the dragon and the wing stalls.","microPassive":"**Iron Scale Discipline:** Units fight at full strength in orthodox formation; isolated from command, they collapse into hysterical rout.","macroPassive":"**Martial Annexation:** Villages within a day's march are placed under martial law; food, labor and refugees are requisitioned by decree.","exemplarNpc":"**Highlord Verminaard, Red Wing Commander**<br>*\"The Queen gives order to a world that has none.\"* Receives a surrendering mayor with cold courtesy, orders his hostages sorted by usefulness, and takes the oath of those who beg.","genericName":"The Imperial Legion","occupant":"Red Dragonarmy under Highlord Verminaard (Draconian line cohorts)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.5; AC-04 §3.1","exemplarInvented":false},"[1, 4, 4]":{"s":1,"e":4,"c":4,"tag":"[1, 4, 4]","archetypeName":"The Draconian Brood","coreBoon":"**Total Conversion:** Stolen metallic eggs become obedient soldiers whose bodies serve as weapons even after death.","coreBurden":"**Decapitation Relapse:** Brood-commanders are the only voices the brood obeys; slay the Aurak or Bozak lead and the squad stops thinking.","microPassive":"**Death-Throe Network:** Fallen draconians petrify, melt or burst into shrapnel; the unit's last act feeds its neighbors' wrath.","macroPassive":"**Clutch Blight:** Hatcheries poison the surrounding earth; stolen eggs, slave labor and temple rites feed an expanding ring of corruption.","exemplarNpc":"**Dracart, Artificer of the Corrupted Clutch**<br>*\"Every shell is a soldier. Every soldier a prayer.\"* Shows a visitor the altar of shattered shells with clinical pride; offers a draconian embryo as proof of loyalty.","genericName":"The Biomechanical Hive","occupant":"Sanction egg-corruption labs and the draconian cohorts they hatch","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"AC-03 §5.1–5.2","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 1, 1]":{"s":2,"e":1,"c":1,"tag":"[2, 1, 1]","archetypeName":"The Hedge-School of Theobald","coreBoon":"**Rote Foundations:** Every apprentice leaves able to read, cast basic cantrips and keep a spellbook, whatever their gift.","coreBurden":"**Pedantic Arrogance:** Dismisses what the textbook omits; a prodigy is a threat, an anomaly is a lie.","microPassive":"**Scholastic Rigor:** Cataloged cantrips never fail inside the schoolhouse; anything beyond the assigned tier fumbles with penalties.","macroPassive":"**Tuition Monopoly:** Regional gentry send sons here; ambitious local youth are discouraged from seeking the Towers or other teachers.","exemplarNpc":"**Master Theobald, Headmaster of the School for Mages**<br>*\"According to the primer, that cannot occur.\"* Corrects the party's grammar and dismisses a monster they just killed because his folio omits it; yields to flattery and to the name of a powerful sponsor.","genericName":"The Hermetic Academy","occupant":"Master Theobald's Academy of Magic near Solace","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.4, §3.3","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 1, 2]":{"s":2,"e":1,"c":2,"tag":"[2, 1, 2]","archetypeName":"The Whitestone Parley","coreBoon":"**Sworn Neutral Ground:** The glade holds delegations from rival nations under a common ceasefire; envoys bring arms but cannot draw them.","coreBurden":"**Procedure Before Peril:** Seven delegations, seven demands and a written order of speaking mean any urgent action waits for adjournment.","microPassive":"**Sanctuary Covenant:** Violence inside the glade triggers coordinated sanction from the assembled powers; disarmed envoys speak freely.","macroPassive":"**Neutral Haven Aura:** Nations bound by the council observe ceasefire lines on neighboring roads; infractions invite embargo.","exemplarNpc":"**Lord Gunthar uth Wistan, Acting Grand Master, Order of the Rose**<br>*\"Draw a blade here and every delegation turns on you.\"* Meets envoys with courtesy, collecting their weapons into locked cases and warning them that the glade's peace ends at the first drawn sword.","genericName":"The Federated Sanctuary","occupant":"Whitestone Council of free nations on Sancrist","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §9","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 1, 3]":{"s":2,"e":1,"c":3,"tag":"[2, 1, 3]","archetypeName":"The Conclave of Three Robes","coreBoon":"**The Test and the Oath:** Lethal trials and ironclad oaths ensure every mage answers to the Art; renegades are hunted and destroyed.","coreBurden":"**Magic Above All:** Treats nations, races and individual lives as secondary to the preservation of the Art; will let a city fall to save a spell.","microPassive":"**Tower Law:** Within the Tower, mages cannot be forced to break an oath; contested arcane works are adjudicated in the chamber with binding runes.","macroPassive":"**Renegade Interdict:** Unsanctioned casting within the Conclave's sphere draws hunters, wards and a summons to the Test.","exemplarNpc":"**Par-Salian, Head of the Conclave, White Robes**<br>*\"The Art outlasts every kingdom.\"* Demands a trial for a promising youth, knowing the cost, and justifies the cruelty with the coming storm.","genericName":"The Curia Network","occupant":"Conclave of Wizards at the Tower of Wayreth (White, Red and Black Robes)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.3, §3.1; AC-03 §3.3–3.4","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 1, 4]":{"s":2,"e":1,"c":4,"tag":"[2, 1, 4]","archetypeName":"The Guild-Bound Mountain","coreBoon":"**Total Guild Coverage:** Every craft, procedure and invention has a guild, a rulebook and a complete record; nothing is lost.","coreBurden":"**The Committee Loop:** A simple device requires approval from every guild; urgent need dies in review.","microPassive":"**Statutory Invention:** Each device follows the Guild Code; failure is documented, cataloged and referred to a sub-committee for redesign.","macroPassive":"**Canonical Contagion:** Neighboring settlements adopt gnomish measures, tools and legal forms to access their machines, and cannot easily leave.","exemplarNpc":"**Gnosh, Chair of the High Council of Inventors**<br>*\"The device is perfect. The committee has not yet approved it.\"* Offers an experimental catapult, three pages of mandatory waivers and a promise that the review will conclude in time for the next war.","genericName":"The Ecclesiastical State","occupant":"Gnomes of Mount Nevermind (guilds, committees, Life Quest)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §9, §11 (source scored [1,2,4], Adhocracy)","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 2, 1]":{"s":2,"e":2,"c":1,"tag":"[2, 2, 1]","archetypeName":"The Barony Hearth","coreBoon":"**Self-Contained Realm:** Smiths, weavers and tanners keep the barony fed, shod and armed through any winter without outside trade.","coreBurden":"**Parochial Honor:** Local custom outranks imperial law or outside appeal; the baron's oath binds more tightly than any treaty.","microPassive":"**Charter of Oath:** Barony residents keep the Solamnic Oath without bureaucratic supervision; discipline is personal and cheap.","macroPassive":"**Green-Valley Order:** The surrounding valley follows the baron's customs, tolls and bison crest by habit, not by compulsion.","exemplarNpc":"**Baron Ivor of Langtree, Lord of the Horned Bison**<br>*\"Honor is my life; the contract is the rest of it.\"* Fights on foot beside his infantry and refuses an unjust contract even when the coin is good.","genericName":"The Chartered Freehold","occupant":"Langtree barony and its self-sufficient winter economy","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"BA-01 §2 Faction 1","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 2, 2]":{"s":2,"e":2,"c":2,"tag":"[2, 2, 2]","archetypeName":"The Unspoiled City","coreBoon":"**Untouched Calm:** Marble streets, silk markets and opera seasons continue unbroken, and the city's wealth is intact.","coreBurden":"**Paralyzing Complacency:** The Senate will not mobilize until dragons darken the bay; war taxes and conscription fail repeatedly.","microPassive":"**Civic Routine:** Daily life, trade and festival calendars run to custom; deviation requires a Senate motion.","macroPassive":"**Deliberate Denial:** Surrounding villages are encouraged to treat the war as a distant barbarian brawl; neighbors' calls for help are politely tabled.","exemplarNpc":"**Lord Amothus, Lord of Palanthas**<br>*\"The war is regrettable. The opera is at eight.\"* Receives a refugee delegation with refreshments and a tabled motion, and cannot be hurried by blood on a visitor's cloak.","genericName":"The Agricultural Shire","occupant":"Palanthas Patrician Senate and Lord Amothus","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.2; AC-04 §4.5","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 2, 3]":{"s":2,"e":2,"c":3,"tag":"[2, 2, 3]","archetypeName":"The Court of the Sun","coreBoon":"**Open-Air Order:** Elegant architecture, shared water and a single royal court give Qualinost a smooth, sun-warm civic order.","coreBurden":"**Noblesse Isolation:** Quietly disdains outsiders and half-blood kin; sacrifices neighbors to save its own bloodline.","microPassive":"**Royal Protocol:** Court ritual and caste etiquette hold the nation steady; breaches are corrected with tact, then exile.","macroPassive":"**Sylvan Border:** The surrounding forest's roads and bridges are patrolled and gently enforced; strangers are watched, not welcomed.","exemplarNpc":"**Speaker Solostaran, Speaker of the Suns**<br>*\"Our people are what remains. They must remain.\"* Weighs refugees as obligations, not allies, and will trade rescue for rescue but never for blood.","genericName":"The Defensive Commonwealth","occupant":"Qualinesti nation under Speaker Solostaran (peacetime Qualinost)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.3","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 2, 4]":{"s":2,"e":2,"c":4,"tag":"[2, 2, 4]","archetypeName":"The Solamnic War Council","coreBoon":"**Combined Arms Doctrine:** Knights, militia, elven archers and dragon wings plan under one chain of command and one set of oaths.","coreBurden":"**Measure Versus Maneuver:** Traditionalists refuse any order not documented in the Measure, delaying blows precisely when speed matters.","microPassive":"**Oath-Bound Cohesion:** Knights and militia obey the council's orders under dragonfear; morale saves improve under a deployed Dragonlance.","macroPassive":"**Citadel Authority:** The council's decrees govern neighboring ports, roads and garrisons; grain and gold flow to the front.","exemplarNpc":"**Lord Ambor, Knight of the Sword, Traditionalist**<br>*\"Show me the precedent, or sit down.\"* Insists on the 37-point parley protocol and bristles when an elven woman is named to command.","genericName":"The Constitutional Republic","occupant":"Kalaman Citadel and the reformed Solamnic War Council","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.1 (source scored [2,2,4])","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 3, 1]":{"s":2,"e":3,"c":1,"tag":"[2, 3, 1]","archetypeName":"The Haven Counting-Houses","coreBoon":"**Private Credit:** Independent merchant houses can finance a caravan, a mercenary or a bribe within a day, on the strength of a sealed note.","coreBurden":"**No Common Front:** Each house guards its own ledger; when the temple demands a tithe, none will risk the first refusal.","microPassive":"**Guild Seal:** Contracts sealed by a recognized house are legally binding; disputes go to the council, not the street.","macroPassive":"**Credit Gravity:** Surrounding towns borrow, rent and trade on Haven's terms, tightly bound to its markets.","exemplarNpc":"**An Alderman of Haven, Master of the Counting-House**<br>*\"I have no politics. I have a ledger.\"* Offers a safe-conduct for payment and will quietly sell out the party if the temple pays better.","genericName":"The Merchant Banking House","occupant":"Haven aldermen and merchant houses","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §3.2","exemplarInvented":true},"[2, 3, 2]":{"s":2,"e":3,"c":2,"tag":"[2, 3, 2]","archetypeName":"The Dust-Port Consortium","coreBoon":"**Open Ledgers:** Every merchant house trades freely with every power; cargo, rumor and cash flow with little friction.","coreBurden":"**Cannot Believe in Enemies:** The council assumes every power has a price; an enemy who cannot be bought is not recognized until too late.","microPassive":"**Tariff Order:** Trade law, harbor charges and guild rank are codified; stranded galleons are tenements and warehouses.","macroPassive":"**Dust-Caravan Tolls:** The overland roads from the stranded harbor carry Tarsis's tariffs; foreign agents and Knights' insignia are arrested at the gates.","exemplarNpc":"**The Governor of Tarsis, Ruler of the Hall of the Guilds**<br>*\"The Dragonarmies are a market like any other.\"* Signs a surrender treaty as a trade agreement and threatens to arrest anyone who calls the dragons real.","genericName":"The Trade Port Consortium","occupant":"Tarsis the Beautiful: Governor and Merchant Council","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §3; AC-04 §4.4","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 3, 3]":{"s":2,"e":3,"c":3,"tag":"[2, 3, 3]","archetypeName":"The Forge-Temple Combine","coreBoon":"**Gold-Vault Logistics:** Temple smiths, caravans and heavy infantry share a single scheduled supply line that keeps the mountain armed.","coreBurden":"**Tariff Piety:** Every concession is demanded at a price in iron or favor; alliances fail when the account is not settled.","microPassive":"**Synchronized Forge:** Armor, arms and stores move to a rhythm tied to Reorx's calendar; downtime is rare.","macroPassive":"**Vault Leverage:** Neighboring clans must buy or borrow from the Daewar vaults; credit becomes a lever of loyalty.","exemplarNpc":"**A Daewar Thane, Master of the Gold-Vaults**<br>*\"Reorx teaches that every debt is paid in the end.\"* Votes with the Upper Bloc but demands trade concessions in return.","genericName":"The Logistical Trust","occupant":"Daewar merchant-warriors of Thorbardin","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §2 (Daewar)","exemplarInvented":true},"[2, 3, 4]":{"s":2,"e":3,"c":4,"tag":"[2, 3, 4]","archetypeName":"The Steel Standard Exchange","coreBoon":"**Universal Utility Coin:** Steel is accepted from the Newsea to Sanction; any weapon-grade ingot can be turned into food, passage or loyalty.","coreBurden":"**Single-Point Collapse:** Iron mines, foundries and caravans are interdependent; when Pax Tharkas falls, the price of steel convulses across the continent.","microPassive":"**Standard Weight:** Merchants on the network use shared weights and measures; disputes are resolved by assay.","macroPassive":"**Steel Pull:** Settlements without iron find themselves subordinated to those who have it; gold-rich cities discover their coin is decorative.","exemplarNpc":"**A Factor of the Steel Exchange, Assayer at the Crossroads**<br>*\"Gold is pretty. Steel pays the bill.\"* Weighs a stranger's coin, notes the origin, and quotes the day's rate for a night's lodging.","genericName":"The Continental Trade Matrix","occupant":"Ansalon-wide steel-piece currency and barter network","sourceStatus":"derived","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AC-04 §5.1","exemplarInvented":true},"[2, 4, 1]":{"s":2,"e":4,"c":1,"tag":"[2, 4, 1]","archetypeName":"The Seeker Chapterhouse","coreBoon":"**Chartered Dominion:** Garrison, tithe and inquisition give the chapterhouse unquestioned local power with no outside oversight.","coreBurden":"**Fear of Haven:** The chapter's authority depends on a distant council; exposure of its false miracles or a refugee's relic would bring ruin.","microPassive":"**Inquisitorial Routine:** Curfews, tithes and public trials run to schedule; dissent is processed rather than debated.","macroPassive":"**Spiritual Insurance Racket:** Local trade, travelers and farmers pay protection for permits and prayers that guard them from the chapter itself.","exemplarNpc":"**High Theocrat Hederick, Seeker Chapter Head, Solace**<br>*\"The gods are silent. I am not.\"* Torments blasphemers in the square, collaborates with the Red Wing when it arrives, and breaks down if his guards are removed.","genericName":"The Colonial Charter Company","occupant":"Solace chapter of the Seeker Theocracy (High Theocrat Hederick)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.1 (source: Hierarchy)","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 4, 2]":{"s":2,"e":4,"c":2,"tag":"[2, 4, 2]","archetypeName":"The Mad Baron's Company","coreBoon":"**Professional Fraternity:** Veterans mentor recruits, share rations and fight as brothers; the company's contract is a promise, not a pretext.","coreBurden":"**Payroll and Principle:** Needs steady contracts to eat but refuses unjust ones; must balance conscience, coin and the Oath.","microPassive":"**Esprit de Corps:** Soldiers carry luck-charms and march in disciplined order; wounded are treated by company healers.","macroPassive":"**Contract Reach:** Neighboring lords pay for protection or hire the company for raids; the company's presence changes regional borders.","exemplarNpc":"**Baron Ivor of Langtree, Captain of the Horned Bison**<br>*\"The coin is good. The cause is not.\"* Rejects a lucrative contract for an unjust cause, then fights on foot beside the common infantry.","genericName":"The Professional Mercenary Core","occupant":"Baron Ivor's mercenary army (Center, Line, Flank, Archers, Warmage Division)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"BA-01 §2 Faction 1","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 4, 3]":{"s":2,"e":4,"c":3,"tag":"[2, 4, 3]","archetypeName":"The Blue Wing Prefecture","coreBoon":"**Lean Occupation:** A few experienced officers, siege engineers and dragons govern a conquered province through reliable delegation.","coreBurden":"**Decapitation Flight:** If the Highlord is killed or discredited, mercenaries and auxiliaries abandon the field.","microPassive":"**Rigid Field Discipline:** Draconian shock companies obey cleanly, and infiltration cells follow orders to the letter.","macroPassive":"**Provincial Writ:** Conquered towns pay taxes in steel and grain to the wing; local lords hold office at her pleasure.","exemplarNpc":"**Highlord Kitiara uth Matar, Blue Wing Commander**<br>*\"I do not need your loyalty. I need your obedience.\"* Flatters a rival while counting his troops, and weighs every ally by what they can be made to lose.","genericName":"The Territorial Prefecture","occupant":"Blue Dragonarmy under Highlord Kitiara uth Matar","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §10; AC-04 §3.1","exemplarInvented":false},"[2, 4, 4]":{"s":2,"e":4,"c":4,"tag":"[2, 4, 4]","archetypeName":"The Imperial Directorate","coreBoon":"**Overwhelming Mass:** Five wings, tens of thousands of troops and over a hundred dragons move under a single command and a single dread.","coreBurden":"**War of Succession in Waiting:** Every Highlord plots against the others; when the crown leaves Ariakas's brow the army turns inward.","microPassive":"**Elemental Shield:** The Emperor is shielded by the Queen's protection; his guards act on a single whispered word.","macroPassive":"**Dread Radiance:** Populations within the Directorate's reach collapse under dread; refusal to submit marks a region for scorched-earth destruction.","exemplarNpc":"**Emperor Ariakas, Supreme Commander of the Dragonarmies**<br>*\"The crown decides who was right.\"* Rewards a captured hero's head with a province and conducts a council in whispers.","genericName":"The Imperial Directorate","occupant":"Unified Dragonarmies under Emperor Ariakas at Neraka","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.5 (source scored [1,4,1])","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 1, 1]":{"s":3,"e":1,"c":1,"tag":"[3, 1, 1]","archetypeName":"The Master Artificer's Tower","coreBoon":"**Monopoly of the Art:** Lost arcane methods, a sealed tower and a key only the master can carry give unmatched insight in a single locked room.","coreBurden":"**Brilliant Solitude:** No apprentices, allies or institutions; a single mistake or a single enemy ends the work.","microPassive":"**Shoikan Sanctum:** Within the grove and tower, the master's wards, undead guardians and fear aura obey him and only him.","macroPassive":"**The Grove's Reach:** The terrifying oaks and rumor of the tower repel intruders from the neighboring quarter, and make the old city a place of whispered dread.","exemplarNpc":"**Raistlin Majere, Master of the Tower, Black Robes**<br>*\"Knowledge is the only coin that is never debased.\"* Receives a visitor with perfect courtesy, names a price in lost reagents and lost secrets, and pays no regard to anyone's gold.","genericName":"The Master Artificer's Cell","occupant":"Raistlin Majere in the Tower of High Sorcery at Palanthas","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §1; AC-03 §3.5; AC-02 §2.2","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 1, 2]":{"s":3,"e":1,"c":2,"tag":"[3, 1, 2]","archetypeName":"The Neidar Craft-Clans","coreBoon":"**Hand-Craft Fellowship:** Smiths, carvers and miners share tools, trade secrets and meat across scattered holds without a master.","coreBurden":"**The Grudge of the Gates:** Century-old resentment of mountain dwarves blocks alliances even where shared interest is plain.","microPassive":"**Clan Honor:** Hill dwarves in a work-gang cover each other's flaws and carry each other's wounds; shame is rare and heavy.","macroPassive":"**Exiled Frontier:** Neidar waystations and steadings serve as discreet safe houses for refugees, but turn back mountain emissaries at the door.","exemplarNpc":"**Flint Fireforge, Hill Dwarf Smith and Carver**<br>*\"If you call me 'mountain dwarf' once more, I will remember it.\"* Grumbles about elves and kender, then refuses to leave a friend in danger; carves a toy for a child while denying he is soft.","genericName":"The Craft Fellowship","occupant":"Neidar hill dwarves (Flint Fireforge's kin)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §2 (Neidar); AC-02 §2.6","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 1, 3]":{"s":3,"e":1,"c":3,"tag":"[3, 1, 3]","archetypeName":"The Wild-Elf Wood","coreBoon":"**Living Concealment:** Tattooed hunters, totem-beasts and forest spirits move as one with the wood and vanish at will.","coreBurden":"**No Siege, No Written Law:** Lacking walls, ledgers or heavy arms, they cannot hold a position against organized assault.","microPassive":"**Chief by Deed:** Leadership passes to whoever proves it; decisions are made swiftly, and traitors are cast out without trial.","macroPassive":"**Bristling Wilds:** Trails, game and water within the wood are guarded by snares, ambushes and spirit-signs; civilized elves are treated as invaders.","exemplarNpc":"**A Kagonesti Chief, War-Leader of the Deep Wood**<br>*\"The trees keep the old oaths. You have only paper.\"* Appears from nowhere with a bone spear, tests the party's respect for the forest, and offers a guide only to those who ask politely.","genericName":"The Ecological Tribe","occupant":"Kagonesti of Southern Ergoth","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §5","exemplarInvented":true},"[3, 1, 4]":{"s":3,"e":1,"c":4,"tag":"[3, 1, 4]","archetypeName":"The Ice Folk Hearth","coreBoon":"**Shared Meat, Shared Boat:** Ice-boats, seal-oil lamps and shared hunts bind the whole tribe into a single survival machine.","coreBurden":"**Fragile Margin:** One lost boat or one thin winter threatens the whole people; hospitality is a duty and a strain.","microPassive":"**Bone-Armor Fellowship:** Warriors fight and hunt as a unit, covering each other without orders; morale is nearly unbreakable at home.","macroPassive":"**Glacier Command:** The ice-flats within a day's sail are patrolled and hunted; strangers are tested with hunger and cold.","exemplarNpc":"**Harald Haarfagre, Chief of the Ice Folk**<br>*\"Eat, then speak. Hunger lies.\"* Welcomes a guest to the fire according to ancient custom and sets a bone-handled test of strength before the hunt.","genericName":"The Decentralized Kin-Mesh","occupant":"Ice Folk of Icewall Glacier","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §7 (source scored [3,1,2])","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 2, 1]":{"s":3,"e":2,"c":1,"tag":"[3, 2, 1]","archetypeName":"The Groundside Camps","coreBoon":"**Nothing to Lose:** Woodcutters, drifters and day laborers live without permanent obligations and respond to emergencies with improvised courage.","coreBurden":"**Patronized Poverty:** Canopy merchants treat them as expendable; resources and protection are never guaranteed.","microPassive":"**Mud-Level Fellowship:** Shared fires and borrowed tools mean a hurt neighbor is carried, fed and hidden without questions.","macroPassive":"**Edge of the Eaves:** The camps watch the roads and the shadows beneath the vallenwoods; strangers are known before they reach the inn.","exemplarNpc":"**Gilon Majere, Woodcutter of Solace**<br>*\"Work is work. The tree does not care who pays.\"* Offers firewood, a place by the fire and a hush if asked, and lowers his voice whenever a Seeker walks past.","genericName":"The Frontier Outpost","occupant":"Groundside outcasts and transient encampments beneath Solace","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.1","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 2, 2]":{"s":3,"e":2,"c":2,"tag":"[3, 2, 2]","archetypeName":"The Free Canopy Commons","coreBoon":"**Quiet Safety Net:** Neighbors share food, tools and shelter without ceremony; a stranger in need is watched over by the whole town.","coreBurden":"**Fear of the Preacher:** Nervous disdain for spellcasters and zealots makes the town slow to accept necessary but strange help.","microPassive":"**Moot at the Hearth:** Decisions are made by open talk at the inn; elders, craftsmen and barkeeps share equal voice.","macroPassive":"**Open-Door Reputation:** Travelers on the north-south road expect lodging, mild ale and gossip; the town's goodwill secures neutrality in minor disputes.","exemplarNpc":"**Otik Sandath, Innkeeper of the Last Home**<br>*\"Sit. There is spiced potato, and there is always more.\"* Welcomes a stranger with potatoes and ale, then quietly weighs who is following them.","genericName":"The Free Towns League","occupant":"Free Community of Solace and the Inn of the Last Home","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.1, §3.4; AC-04 §4.1","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 2, 3]":{"s":3,"e":2,"c":3,"tag":"[3, 2, 3]","archetypeName":"The Whitestone Alliance","coreBoon":"**Mutual Reliance:** Knights, elven archers, militia and dragons each cover the others' weakness; no single wing can win or lose alone.","coreBurden":"**Alliance Friction:** Pride, grievance and unequal command create constant risk of schism; a slighted delegation can leave overnight.","microPassive":"**Shared Banner:** Units rally under a unifying leader and symbol; morale and reaction speed improve when the commander is present.","macroPassive":"**Liberated Hinterland:** Rescued towns and ports supply grain, labor and goodwill; the army's presence deters nearby raiders.","exemplarNpc":"**Laurana, The Golden General**<br>*\"I am not here to be protected. I am here to lead.\"* Corrects a veteran's tactical error in front of the staff, then asks him to stay and show her what she missed.","genericName":"The Mutualist Network","occupant":"Whitestone Army under Laurana (knights, elves, militia, metallic dragons)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.1, §2.4 (source scored Hierarchy)","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 2, 4]":{"s":3,"e":2,"c":4,"tag":"[3, 2, 4]","archetypeName":"The Refugee Host","coreBoon":"**Every Hand a Guard:** Eight hundred refugees, from miners to mothers, defend each other, watch the passes and carry the wounded.","coreBurden":"**No Reserve:** Food, winter clothing and arms are scarce; one lost pack animal threatens the column's life.","microPassive":"**Shared Peril:** Strangers become kin by survival; panic spreads fast but so does discipline under a trusted leader.","macroPassive":"**Moving Sanctuary:** The column draws Dragonarmy patrols, but also allies and shelter-givers whose pity or pride is stirred.","exemplarNpc":"**Elistan of Haven, Cleric of the Restored Faith**<br>*\"Healing comes to those who believe, not those who are worthy.\"* Blesses the sick with calm, asks for volunteers to guard the passes, and gives every refugee a task.","genericName":"The Citizen Militia Mesh","occupant":"Refugee column of Pax Tharkas (humans, dwarves, Qualinesti children) under Elistan","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.4; WN-01 §1","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 3, 1]":{"s":3,"e":3,"c":1,"tag":"[3, 3, 1]","archetypeName":"The Wildcat Turncoat","coreBoon":"**Profitable Doubt:** One man, many allegiances; secrets and escape routes are sold to whichever party pays best.","coreBurden":"**Trust Is Worthless:** Cannot be loved or relied on; exposure ends him, and the price is paid in blood.","microPassive":"**Charming Bridge:** Smooth talk and a cynical sense of timing let him recruit, mislead and withdraw before a plan unravels.","macroPassive":"**Whisper Market:** Information leaks from the camp he joins; rumors of discord and mistrust follow him down every road.","exemplarNpc":"**Eben Shatterstone, Scion of a Ruined House**<br>*\"Honor is a sucker's game. I intend to win.\"* Sows distrust between elves and humans, then offers his help as the only man who can fix it.","genericName":"The Wildcat Prospector","occupant":"Eben Shatterstone, ruined noble turned double agent","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-02 §4.5; AT-01 §2.5","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 3, 2]":{"s":3,"e":3,"c":2,"tag":"[3, 3, 2]","archetypeName":"The Scrounger's Barter-Ring","coreBoon":"**Everyone Has Something:** Multi-party barter turns surplus cattle, dented armor and hops into legendary bows without a coin moving.","coreBurden":"**Panic Under Plan:** A human mind in a kender frame feels fear acutely; when the bargain fails, the barterer flees.","microPassive":"**Pocket Quartermaster:** The unit's gear, tack and ration lists are known to one person, who can always find the missing piece.","macroPassive":"**Caravan Web:** Dwarven, human and halfling caravans trade surplus through the ring; trouble in one link reaches all.","exemplarNpc":"**Scrounger, Half-Kender Quartermaster**<br>*\"Everyone has something someone else wants. Everyone has something he does not need.\"* Arranges a cattle-for-longbows exchange across three parties and a kender-sized fib.","genericName":"The Independent Caravan","occupant":"Scrounger and the kender/half-kender quartermasters of Company C","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"high","sourceRefs":"BA-01 §2 Faction 4","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 3, 3]":{"s":3,"e":3,"c":3,"tag":"[3, 3, 3]","archetypeName":"The Dragonlance Forge-Venture","coreBoon":"**Pooled Craft Risk:** Smiths, scholars and soldiers pool funds, reagents and nerve to test a weapon no one has made in centuries.","coreBurden":"**Untested Triumph:** A single failure in the forge burns the pooled trust; success multiplies the enemy's attention.","microPassive":"**Joint Workshop:** Shared tools, knowledge and shifts accelerate learning; each failed test is studied by all.","macroPassive":"**Forge Rumor:** Word of the new weapon spreads along trade roads, drawing recruits, saboteurs and Dragonarmy spies.","exemplarNpc":"**Theros Ironfeld, Smith of the First Dragonlance**<br>*\"I forged a weapon. The gods will decide if it is enough.\"* Works the forge by night, refusing coin and asking only that the lance be carried by one who will use it well.","genericName":"The Venture Consortium","occupant":"Theros Ironfeld and the smiths forging the first Dragonlances","sourceStatus":"derived","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §9","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 3, 4]":{"s":3,"e":3,"c":4,"tag":"[3, 3, 4]","archetypeName":"The Waystation Mesh","coreBoon":"**News Before Trouble:** Inns trade gossip, grain and warnings across the whole road in a day.","coreBurden":"**One Betrayal, Whole Net:** An informer in one inn exposes every stop; a burned stable burns the route.","microPassive":"**Shared Cellar:** Staff, stock and secret rooms are interchangeable; a guest is protected anywhere on the chain.","macroPassive":"**Road-Wise Influence:** Travelers learn the network's price, and routes bend around its reliable stops.","exemplarNpc":"**A Roadhouse Keeper, Innkeeper on the Haven Road**<br>*\"I pour the ale. I pass the word.\"* Slides a note under a plate and waits to see who reads it.","genericName":"The Merchant Syndicate Mesh","occupant":"Innkeepers, ostlers and caravan stops linking Haven, Solace and Qualinesti","sourceStatus":"derived","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.1; AC-04 §4.1","exemplarInvented":true},"[3, 4, 1]":{"s":3,"e":4,"c":1,"tag":"[3, 4, 1]","archetypeName":"The Mud-Foot Raiders","coreBoon":"**Opportunistic Ambush:** Dire-wolf scouts hit refugee columns and undefended farms with speed and no loyalty beyond loot.","coreBurden":"**Cowardice and Debt:** They fold at the first serious resistance and cannot be relied on to hold ground.","microPassive":"**Pack Loyalty:** Each band follows the biggest bully; no tactic outlasts the leader's fear.","macroPassive":"**Smoke on the Horizon:** Villages within a day's ride burn or pay; refugees flee ahead of the raiders.","exemplarNpc":"**Fewmaster Toede, Goblin Raid-Captain**<br>*\"Burn it, then tell the Highlord it was a battle.\"* Takes credit for other officers' victories and screams for backup when cornered.","genericName":"The Corsair Privateer","occupant":"Fewmaster Toede's goblin irregulars (wolf-mounted scouts)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.5; AT-02 §4.6","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 4, 2]":{"s":3,"e":4,"c":2,"tag":"[3, 4, 2]","archetypeName":"The Ice-Boat Flotilla","coreBoon":"**Frozen Blockade:** Sail-sleds and walrus-folk strike along the ice, cut supply lanes and retreat before pursuit.","coreBurden":"**Thaw and Hunger:** Dependent on the cold; a warm season or a lost sled costs the raid its legs.","microPassive":"**Cold Camaraderie:** Raiders share bone-armor, seal-fat and oath, enduring weather that routs others.","macroPassive":"**Ice-Lane Tolls:** Coastal and glacial trade pays in goods or fear; ports on the Icewall shore close in winter.","exemplarNpc":"**Highlord Feal-Thas, White Wing Commander**<br>*\"The cold is patient. So am I.\"* Receives captives in an ice-hall and conducts interrogations with no heat but his own.","genericName":"The Raider Flotilla","occupant":"White Dragonarmy under Highlord Feal-Thas (Thanoi, ice-nomads, Sleet)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AC-04 §3.1; WN-01 §7","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 4, 3]":{"s":3,"e":4,"c":3,"tag":"[3, 4, 3]","archetypeName":"The Black Wing Vanguard","coreBoon":"**Amphibious Night Raids:** Lizardfolk, Kapak assassins and swamp-stalking infantry strike from water and dark.","coreBurden":"**Stretched Lines:** Fast expansion outruns supply; the wing's strength is wasted if a flank collapses.","microPassive":"**Silent Cohorts:** Troops move without torches and communicate by touch; discipline is high until the first dawn.","macroPassive":"**Poisoned Wells:** Targeted contamination of water supplies drives settlements to flee or surrender.","exemplarNpc":"**Highlord Lucien of Takar, Black Wing Commander**<br>*\"Water carries everything. Including death.\"* Plans an attack at moonrise, then conceals the army until the sentries are drunk.","genericName":"The Expansionist Vanguard","occupant":"Black Dragonarmy under Highlord Lucien of Takar","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"AC-04 §3.1; SD-01 §2.5","exemplarInvented":false},"[3, 4, 4]":{"s":3,"e":4,"c":4,"tag":"[3, 4, 4]","archetypeName":"The Green Wing Swarm","coreBoon":"**Woodland Swarm:** Goblin legions, ogre shock units and Kapak throat-slitters flood the forest edges and overwhelm defenders by numbers.","coreBurden":"**Poison and Panic:** The swarm depends on its poisons and a green dragon's whim; destroy the dragon and the swarm scatters.","microPassive":"**Shared Frenzy:** The swarm's mood is contagious; a charge becomes unstoppable until it breaks.","macroPassive":"**Dream Blight:** Forests near the wing sicken; settlements find their nights haunted by fever and false visions.","exemplarNpc":"**Highlord Salah-Khan, Green Wing Commander**<br>*\"The forest falls. Then the people.\"* Counts the wing's casualties as a cost of doing business, and enjoys the dream-blight.","genericName":"The Predatory Swarm","occupant":"Green Dragonarmy under Salah-Khan and Cyan Bloodbane (goblin/ogre swarm, Kapak, poison)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AC-04 §3.1","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 1, 1]":{"s":4,"e":1,"c":1,"tag":"[4, 1, 1]","archetypeName":"The Gray Wanderer","coreBoon":"**Fumbling Miracle:** Erratic spells and impossible luck turn the worst moment into the right one, for reasons no mortal can predict.","coreBurden":"**Sworn Non-Intervention:** May advise, console and nudge but never overrule mortal free will; will not save those who must save themselves.","microPassive":"**Absent-Minded Cloak:** Appears harmless to anyone watching; foes underestimate him until a spell finds its mark.","macroPassive":"**Quiet Providence:** Wherever he wanders, small kindnesses and strange coincidences gather, nudging travelers toward their own courage.","exemplarNpc":"**Fizban the Fabulous, Old Wizard in Mouse-Gray Robes**<br>*\"Now, where did I put that hat?\"* Mumbles spell components, hands the party the correct answer by accident, and refuses to say whether he meant it.","genericName":"The Volatile Hermit","occupant":"Fizban the Fabulous (Paladine in mortal guise), bound by divine non-interference","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AC-03 §1.3; AT-02 §3.3","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 1, 2]":{"s":4,"e":1,"c":2,"tag":"[4, 1, 2]","archetypeName":"The Renegade Circle","coreBoon":"**Untested Power:** Casting without oath or Test, they invent spells no tower allows.","coreBurden":"**Marked for the Hunt:** The Conclave and the Seekers both hunt them; any careless cantrip may bring an execution.","microPassive":"**Hidden Lab:** A cellar, a tinker's cart or a forest hollow serves as workshop; secrecy is the whole defense.","macroPassive":"**Hedge-Rumor:** Peasants whisper of a miracle-worker nearby; the Seekers hear it too.","exemplarNpc":"**A Renegade Hedge-Mage, Untested Caster in Hiding**<br>*\"They would kill me for this. I do it anyway.\"* Heals a child with a forbidden spell and then asks the party to help her flee before the Seekers arrive.","genericName":"The Rogue Alchemical Cell","occupant":"Renegade mages hunted by the Conclave","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.3; AC-03 §3.3","exemplarInvented":true},"[4, 1, 3]":{"s":4,"e":1,"c":3,"tag":"[4, 1, 3]","archetypeName":"The Aghar Warrens","coreBoon":"**Hole-Knowledge:** Every pipe, chute and rat-run beneath a ruin is mapped in collective memory and shared at need.","coreBurden":"**Groveling Survival:** Cannot count past two, plan past tomorrow or resist a single shouted order.","microPassive":"**Pack Panic:** The warren scatters at the first threat and regroups without a word; losses are rarely fatal and always forgotten.","macroPassive":"**Sewer Tolerance:** Larger powers leave the Aghar alone because they are beneath notice; informants hide in their tunnels.","exemplarNpc":"**Bupu Bulp, Royal Shamaness of the Aghar**<br>*\"You is nice. Bupu help.\"* Gives a stranger a poultice of pond slime and loyalty for life if treated with gentle dignity.","genericName":"The Shifting Tribe","occupant":"Aghar (gully dwarves) of Xak Tsaroth and the Pax Tharkas mines","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.4; WN-01 §2 (Aghar)","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 1, 4]":{"s":4,"e":1,"c":4,"tag":"[4, 1, 4]","archetypeName":"The Dream Made Flesh","coreBoon":"**Shape of Fear:** The realm becomes a living instrument; every leaf, stone and breath shapes itself to the dreamer's terror.","coreBurden":"**No Waking:** Inhabitants cannot tell wake from sleep; the only way out is to break the dream or die in it.","microPassive":"**Dream-Logic Flux:** Walls bleed, trees speak with human voices, and allies become enemies without warning; everyone shares the same delirium.","macroPassive":"**Marble Charnel:** The surrounding forest corrodes; refugees, rescuers and even invaders are drawn into the same pattern.","exemplarNpc":"**Cyan Bloodbane, Green Dragon Dreamweaver**<br>*\"Your fear is a garden. I merely water it.\"* Whispers through a sleeping king's mind and presents the nightmare as the only way to save his people.","genericName":"The Metamorphic Hive","occupant":"Silvanesti under Cyan Bloodbane's nightmare (the crisis-metamorphosis of the Dreaming Court)","sourceStatus":"crisis-state","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §4; AC-04 §4.3","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 2, 1]":{"s":4,"e":2,"c":1,"tag":"[4, 2, 1]","archetypeName":"The Wayfaring Rangers","coreBoon":"**Anywhere Welcome:** A traveler with no home can find a hearth in any town and a path through any wood.","coreBurden":"**No Ties:** Belongs nowhere; when trouble comes, no one is obliged to stand beside them.","microPassive":"**Trail-Wise Judgment:** Instincts for terrain, danger and character help a lone ranger lead a band without a command structure.","macroPassive":"**Road Rumor:** News, favors and warnings spread through the ranger's network along the trails.","exemplarNpc":"**Tanis Half-Elven, Wandering Ranger and Mercenary**<br>*\"I am neither one thing nor the other.\"* Chooses neutrality when a decision is needed, and tries to bridge the people he cannot join.","genericName":"The Free Drifter","occupant":"Itinerant rangers, bards and half-elf wanderers","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-01 §2.1; AT-02 §2.1","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 2, 2]":{"s":4,"e":2,"c":2,"tag":"[4, 2, 2]","archetypeName":"The Sivak Phantom Cell","coreBoon":"**Borrowed Faces:** Shapeshifters impersonate sentries, couriers and commanders, delivering false orders in the dark.","coreBurden":"**Death Reveals:** When slain they assume the killer's likeness, sowing confusion but revealing the cell.","microPassive":"**Cell Silence:** Each Sivak knows only its handler and its mark; capture reveals little.","macroPassive":"**Doubt Contagion:** Armies facing Sivak cells begin to suspect every ally; paranoia spreads faster than any rumor.","exemplarNpc":"**A Sivak Infiltrator, Winged Assassin in a Courier's Cloak**<br>*\"Do you recognize my face? You should.\"* Delivers a forged order with perfect handwriting and waits for the party to act on it.","genericName":"The Phantom Cell","occupant":"Sivak infiltrators of the Blue Wing","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §10; AC-03 §5.2","exemplarInvented":true},"[4, 2, 3]":{"s":4,"e":2,"c":3,"tag":"[4, 2, 3]","archetypeName":"The Belzor Flock","coreBoon":"**Fervent Wave:** Grieving widows, impoverished farmers and ruined craftsmen gather by the hundred when the priests call, giving the cult a mob on demand.","coreBurden":"**Hunger for a Miracle:** The flock cannot be reasoned with; when the miracle fails, rage turns on the nearest heretic.","microPassive":"**Shared Fire:** One person's testimony ignites the rest; fear and hope spread quickly through the crowd.","macroPassive":"**Torch and Stake:** The flock burns suspected mages and poisons the water of unbelievers within a day's march.","exemplarNpc":"**A Grieving Widow of Haven, Believer in Belzor**<br>*\"He spoke to me. He said my son would live.\"* Offers the party her last coin and her last prayer, and will denounce them if they mock the faith.","genericName":"The Populist Wildfire","occupant":"Fanatical commoners of the Cult of Belzor","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.2","exemplarInvented":true},"[4, 2, 4]":{"s":4,"e":2,"c":4,"tag":"[4, 2, 4]","archetypeName":"The Bonded Flight","coreBoon":"**Soul-Bond:** Rider and dragon share breath, sight and resolve; a lance in a bonded rider's hand strikes true.","coreBurden":"**Sovereign Pride:** Each dragon is a free agent who may leave when the bond is dishonored or the cause is ignoble.","microPassive":"**Two Hearts, One Will:** Damage, fear and fatigue are shared across rider and mount; both survive or both fall.","macroPassive":"**Radiant Sky:** The presence of a bonded flight rallies nearby troops and terrifies chromatic wings.","exemplarNpc":"**Silvara, Silver Dragon in Elven Form**<br>*\"A bond is not a leash.\"* Tests the rider's honor before agreeing to carry them, and leaves at once if she senses cruelty.","genericName":"The Living Symbiont Collective","occupant":"Metallic dragons and their soul-bonded Dragonlance riders","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.4","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 3, 1]":{"s":4,"e":3,"c":1,"tag":"[4, 3, 1]","archetypeName":"The Kender Wayfarers","coreBoon":"**Fearless Curiosity:** Immune to dragonfear and bored by caution, they wander into places no sensible traveler will go and come back with maps.","coreBurden":"**Loose Fingers, Loose Tongue:** Cannot stop borrowing or exaggerating; every promise is sincere and every possession temporary.","microPassive":"**Cheerful Disruption:** A kender in the room breaks tension, stalls an interrogation and derails a plan with equal ease.","macroPassive":"**Tall-Tale Currency:** Stories, trinkets and rumors from a kender spread faster than official news, changing the mood of a town.","exemplarNpc":"**Tasslehoff Burrfoot, Kender Wanderer**<br>*\"I only borrowed it. I was going to give it back.\"* Pulls a priceless artifact from a pocket, tells a story about it that is half true, and has no idea he has changed history.","genericName":"The Master Charlatan","occupant":"Kender (Tasslehoff Burrfoot and his kin)","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-02 §2.7; AC-02 §2.5","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 3, 2]":{"s":4,"e":3,"c":2,"tag":"[4, 3, 2]","archetypeName":"The Theiwar Shadow-Web","coreBoon":"**Poison and Secret Passage:** Savant sorcery, poisoncraft and unmapped tunnels give them silent reach through the mountain.","coreBurden":"**Daylight and Exposure:** Their treachery lives in secrecy; exposed, they lose allies at once.","microPassive":"**Cell Confidence:** Plans are known to few; betrayal is rare because the cost is death.","macroPassive":"**Smuggled Loyalty:** Dragonarmy envoys, black-market dealers and rival thanes pass messages and goods through Theiwar hands.","exemplarNpc":"**Thane Realgar, Theiwar Lord**<br>*\"Your secret is safe with me. For a price.\"* Meets in a lightless gallery, demands platinum or dark scrolls, and offers non-aggression pacts that favor only himself.","genericName":"The Shadow Smuggler Network","occupant":"Theiwar dark dwarves and their secret pacts","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §2 (Theiwar)","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 3, 3]":{"s":4,"e":3,"c":3,"tag":"[4, 3, 3]","archetypeName":"The Charlatan Circuit","coreBoon":"**Instant Market:** A wagon train becomes a bazaar in an hour; goods, news and cheap miracles are sold before the mob wakes up.","coreBurden":"**Ready to Flee:** Every troupe knows how to pack and run; the crowd's anger rises faster than the coin does.","microPassive":"**Improvised Craft:** Acts, tricks and tonics are made on the spot; a failed trick is turned into a new one.","macroPassive":"**Credulity Tax:** Villages along the circuit pay for entertainment and false hope, and the Seekers hate the competition.","exemplarNpc":"**Waylan the Illusionist, Showman of the Haven Fair**<br>*\"Step right up, step right up, the miracle is in the bottle!\"* Sells peppermint-and-grain tonic as the cure for plague and slips out before the buyers wake.","genericName":"The Chaos Bazaar","occupant":"Itinerant carnivals, illusionists and tonic-sellers","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SF-01 §2.5","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 3, 4]":{"s":4,"e":3,"c":4,"tag":"[4, 3, 4]","archetypeName":"The Orb Frenzy","coreBoon":"**Common Obsession:** Rival nations suddenly share a single desire, bridging old grievances with a grim momentary unity.","coreBurden":"**Auction of Doom:** Elves claim it as ancestral, knights as salvage, dwarves condemn it and merchants try to buy it; blades are drawn.","microPassive":"**Contagious Greed:** Fear and covetousness spread among the delegates; the loudest voice sets the room's mood.","macroPassive":"**Mania Radiance:** Nations hear of the relic and begin to bid, hoard and spy; rumors become treaties and treaties become wars.","exemplarNpc":"**Derek Crownguard, Bearer of the Orb**<br>*\"It is mine by right. Mine.\"* Carries the relic into council and refuses to part with it, certain it will save the Knighthood.","genericName":"The Speculative Mania","occupant":"Whitestone delegations under the influence of the Dragon Orb","sourceStatus":"crisis-state","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"WN-01 §9","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 4, 1]":{"s":4,"e":4,"c":1,"tag":"[4, 4, 1]","archetypeName":"The Wyrm in the Ruin","coreBoon":"**Apex Hoard:** A solitary ancient predator rules a ruined city with acid, darkness and unsleeping paranoia.","coreBurden":"**Trapped by Her Hoard:** Cannot leave her pile; every intruder is a thief and every sound a threat.","microPassive":"**Submerged Ambush:** Water, shadow and corrosive spit give the lair a lethal rhythm: strike from below, vanish, repeat.","macroPassive":"**Terror of the Drowned City:** Nearby settlements dare not enter the ruin; Aghar slaves keep the lifts running out of fear.","exemplarNpc":"**Khisanth, Black Dragon of Xak Tsaroth**<br>*\"Mine. All of it. Mine.\"* Speaks only to taunt, and attacks the moment a visitor reaches for the hoard.","genericName":"The Lone Apex Predator","occupant":"Khisanth (Onyx) in flooded Xak Tsaroth","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"AT-02 §4.3","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 4, 2]":{"s":4,"e":4,"c":2,"tag":"[4, 4, 2]","archetypeName":"The Slave-Takers' Drive","coreBoon":"**Blood-Money Momentum:** Plunder, slaves and quotas pay the wing's bonuses and keep the war going.","coreBurden":"**Mutiny of Loot:** Soldiers loyal only to plunder will turn on each other when the hoard is split.","microPassive":"**Raider's Rhythm:** Fast scouts, hobgoblin whips and holding pens keep the column moving; stragglers are left behind.","macroPassive":"**Empty Villages:** Towns along the drive are stripped of labor; refugees spread panic faster than the column can march.","exemplarNpc":"**Commander Kholos, Half-Goblin Plunder-Captain**<br>*\"Everything is mine. Sort it by value.\"* Executes looters for the Highlord's benefit and takes the best loot for himself.","genericName":"The Feral Corsair Crew","occupant":"Plunder bands and slave-drives marching captives to Sanction and Neraka","sourceStatus":"derived","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"BA-01 §2 Faction 3","exemplarInvented":false},"[4, 4, 3]":{"s":4,"e":4,"c":3,"tag":"[4, 4, 3]","archetypeName":"The Plains-Host of Neraka","coreBoon":"**Overwhelming Numbers:** Tens of thousands of expendable troops flood any front and make attrition a victory.","coreBurden":"**Ravening Without Plan:** Without an iron hand, the host falls on itself over food, loot and old grudges.","microPassive":"**Mob Courage:** Courage grows with numbers; a single charge can be a stampede.","macroPassive":"**Locust Line:** The plains within reach are stripped of grain and cattle; the host's presence turns settled land into wasteland.","exemplarNpc":"**A Hobgoblin Warlord, Chief of the Plains-Host**<br>*\"More for us. Less for them.\"* Pledges loyalty to the Highlord, then quarrels with his neighbor over a stolen cow.","genericName":"The Scavenger Horde","occupant":"Goblin, ogre and human mercenary legions bivouacked outside Neraka","sourceStatus":"direct","confidence":"medium","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §2.5","exemplarInvented":true},"[4, 4, 4]":{"s":4,"e":4,"c":4,"tag":"[4, 4, 4]","archetypeName":"The Maelstrom of Istar","coreBoon":"**Tidal Annihilation:** A constant storm destroys fleets, relics and whole coasts without cost to itself.","coreBurden":"**Consumes What It Feeds:** Can neither be commanded nor contained; its fury follows its own caprice.","microPassive":"**Spiral Dissolution:** Everything inside the vortex is pulled into the same pattern; nothing keeps its shape for long.","macroPassive":"**Red-Sea Blight:** The surrounding water is poisoned; sailors steer far around it, and rumors of the sunken Kingpriest's city draw the foolish.","exemplarNpc":"**Zeboim, Sea Witch, Goddess of Storms**<br>*\"Drown, then. I do not mind.\"* Appears in the foam as a woman of storm-grey hair and sends a wave to answer any insult.","genericName":"The Entropic Vortex","occupant":"The Blood Sea vortex over drowned Istar (Zeboim's storm)","sourceStatus":"crisis-state","confidence":"low","sourceRefs":"SD-01 §1; AC-03 §2.1–2.2","exemplarInvented":false}}}};
